    { q: 'Does PRA have its own specific late-filing penalty structure?', a: 'Yes — distinct from FBR\'s federal structure and other provinces\' frameworks, so confirm PRA\'s own current published penalty schedule rather than assuming a shared figure across authorities.' },
    { q: 'Does a Punjab business need a PRA-specific accountant, or can a general tax consultant handle it?', a: 'A tax consultant with specific PRA experience is valuable given the portal and procedural specifics involved, though this is a service, not a separate professional qualification requirement.' },
    { q: 'Can PRA filing be delegated to a junior staff member once the process is set up?', a: 'Yes, once a clear, documented process exists — though periodic oversight from someone senior remains worthwhile to catch any drift in accuracy over time.' },
    { q: 'Does PRA ever conduct its own review or audit of a registered business\'s filings?', a: 'Yes — provincial authorities can conduct their own review activity similar in principle to an FBR audit, which is another reason maintaining accurate, well-documented monthly records matters beyond just the filing itself.' },
    { q: 'Is there a way to see a history of all past PRA filings in one place through the portal?', a: 'PRA\'s portal generally provides some form of filing history and status view — reviewing this periodically helps confirm past filings were properly received and processed.' },
    { q: 'Does a business need to renew its PRA registration periodically, or is it a one-time registration?', a: 'Confirm PRA\'s current specific rules on this — some registrations remain valid indefinitely as long as the business stays active and compliant, while others may involve periodic renewal or confirmation steps.' },
    { q: 'Does closing a Punjab business location require formally deregistering with PRA?', a: 'Yes — a business ceasing its taxable services activity should formally address its PRA registration status rather than simply stopping filings, since an unresolved registration can continue accruing obligations on paper.' },
    { q: 'Does PRA distinguish between a sole proprietor and a company for registration purposes?', a: 'The registration process generally accommodates different business structures, though the specific documentation required can differ — confirm the applicable requirements for your specific business structure.' }
